clips: real
look: vintage
---
You'll never know how many times an ordinary moment kept you safe.
We spend so much energy being upset about the small stuff.
Running late. Forgetting something. Plans falling through.
And we call it a bad day.

You go back inside for something you forgot, and leave five minutes later than you planned.
You cancel at the last minute because you're just too tired.
You take the long way home for no real reason.

But most of those moments don't mean anything.
And a few of them might mean everything.
You just never get to see the version of the day that didn't happen.

Not every delay is bad luck.
Not every change of plans is a loss.
Some days, late is just late.
Other days, late is the reason you made it home.
And if something bad did happen to you, it wasn't because you chose wrong.
Life doesn't work like that.

Be a little gentler with the ordinary days. You never know what they carried you past.
